          "discrepancies": "1) Reported change “Test locks” is not present in DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 4 visible content for v1.63.0.\n2) Reported change about “Locate across frames with frame locators” is not present in DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 4 visible content.\n3) Reported change “Visible-only locators” / “locator.visible()” is not present in DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 4 visible content.\n4) The DOM does show other distinct changes (httpCredentials array support; dialogclosed events; ariaSnapshotJSON APIs; --add-reporter behavior), which suggests the agent may have inferred or sourced the three listed items from elsewhere/not from the evidenced DOM segment.",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 4 (https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/releases/tag/v1.63.0)\nVisible release-notes content includes a section labeled “New APIs” with multiple concrete bullet items, e.g.:\n- Under “Browser and Context”: “httpCredentials now also accepts an array of credentials. The first entry matching the request origin is used…”\n- Under “Browser and Context”: “New option includes the in the storage state, so it can be persisted and restored into later contexts.” (with nearby links “origin private file system” / “opfs”)\n- Under “Browser and Context”: “New events and are emitted when a JavaScript dialog is accepted, dismissed or closed by the user.” with links “page.on('dialogclosed')” and “browserContext.on('dialogclosed')”.\n- Under “Locators”: “New locator.ariaSnapshotJSON() and page.ariaSnapshotJSON() return the aria snapshot as a JSON value…” with links “locator.ariaSnapshotJSON()” and “page.ariaSnapshotJSON()”.\n- Under “Test runner”: “New command line option appends a reporter…” (flags shown: “--add-reporter”, “--reporter”).\n\nThis DOM snapshot does NOT show any text about “Test locks”, “Locate across frames with frame locators”, or “Visible-only locators”, nor does it show a publication date or confirm that v1.63.0 is the newest non-preview release; it only evidences that these specific bullet changes are present on the v1.63.0 release page view captured.",
